Third-party components

This product optionally uses, but does not bundle, the following third-party
software. Their licenses apply to their respective works:

- Graphsignal — GPU profiler for AI agents (https://github.com/graphsignal/graphsignal),
  Apache License 2.0. KernelOPT integrates it as an external sidecar (launched via
  `graphsignal-run`) and reads its local `/signals` JSON API. The llama.cpp/NInfer
  launchers used by KernelOPT live in the fork at
  https://github.com/giveen/graphsignal (also Apache License 2.0). No Graphsignal
  source is included in this repository; the profiler is provisioned separately
  into a managed virtual environment.

- Rust crate dependencies (anyhow, clap, serde, serde_json, toml, chrono, uuid,
  reqwest, ctrlc, and their transitive dependencies) are distributed under
  permissive licenses (MIT and/or Apache-2.0). See Cargo.lock and each crate for
  the exact terms.

- The ninfer and llama.cpp source trees are optimization *targets*, not part of
  this work, and are not included here.

This project is an independent implementation of the method described in
"KernelOPT: Dispatch-Aware Agentic Search for GPU Kernel Optimization"
(arXiv:2609.30059). The paper is a separate work and is not included here.
